    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8220A\n\nSPONSOR: RYAN S\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the education law, in relation to reducing tuition rates\nfor certain Olympic athletes\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo provide for in-state tuition at public universities and colleges for\nTeam USA athletes training in New York State.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: amends the education law to define \"Team USA athlete\" and\nstipulates that such individuals will be eligible for in-state tuition\nat SUNY institutions.\n\nSection 2: amends Subdivision 7 of section 6206 of the education law\nsuch that the same benefits are available at the City University of New\nYork.\n\nSection 3: effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nNew York State has a rich Olympic tradition having hosted the Winter\nOlympics at Lake Placid in 1932 and 1980. This bill intends to keep New\nYork competitive with states such as California, Colorado, and Utah that\nprovide in-state tuition to US Olympic athletes in training. Offering\nthis benefit to US Olympic-level athletes will help to further Lake\nPlacid's reputation and increase the likelihood that US elite athletes\nwill choose to study in New York while they continue their training.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the first of July next succeeding the date\non which it shall have become a law.\n",
